# Background Process & Job Control Lab

Log in as "student" (password: student) for each task below.

## 9.3 — Too many background jobs
You've lost track of what's running in the background under your session.
Identify everything running and clean up the background jobs you no
longer need.

## 9.4 — Process won't die with a normal kill
There's a process that keeps surviving a standard `kill`. Figure out why
and actually terminate it.

## 9.5 — High CPU usage from a runaway script
Something is consuming a full CPU core and the system feels sluggish.
Track down the culprit process and deal with it.

## 9.10 — Port already in use
A new service needs to bind to TCP port 8000 but fails, complaining the
address is already in use. Find what's holding the port and free it up.

Useful commands: `jobs`, `ps aux`, `ps -ef --forest`, `top`/`htop`,
`kill`, `kill -9`, `pkill`, `lsof -i :8000`, `ss -tlnp`,
`fuser -k 8000/tcp`.
